t year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 12% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 36% and a beta of 0.79, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.29 vs 5y 0.74), so read it loosely.","About $84.0M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 60% in the 2020 crash and 32% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $17.65 (margin of safety -105%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 29%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $11.45 to $26.76 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 52.5 vs 17.7, EV/EBITDA 15.4 vs 10.5 and P/FCF 22.7 vs 15.8 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 112% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 4.4% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.4% (vs the 8% bar).","The 16 covering analysts target $43.50 on average, 20% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 22% clears the cost of capital of 8.2% by 14pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.37).","It runs a 37% gross margin and converts 10% of revenue into free cash flow.","ROE of 20% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (8.4x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.5% of revenue on R&D and 0.5% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.4x net debt to EBITDA ($163.0M of cash against $1.6B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.5x.","The current ratio of 0.90 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","It runs on negative working capital (-17 days), so customers and suppliers effectively fund its operations."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 12.7% over 3 years and -7.1% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 22%).","At current returns, reinvesting 98% of profits supports about 21.9% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -4.8% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are contracting (-1.4% trend).","Capex runs 1.7x depreciation (11.0% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 2, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","The share count has shrunk 6.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 12.4% of the float, 5.3 days to cover."],"people":["With about 13,000 employees, each generates about $159K of revenue, 0.4x the Consumer Cyclical median.","That works out to $16K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $825K (5x revenue per employee)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":31,"head":"Avoid: priced 105% above its fair value of $17.65.","pros":["ROIC 22.3% vs WACC 8.2%","16 analysts' mean target $43.50 (+20%)"],"cons":["Trades 105% above fair value of $17.65","Revenue shrank 7.1%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 3.4x","Interest coverage only 2.5x","P/E 52.5x vs sector 17.7x"],"flags":["Priced 105% above its fair value of $17.65"],"need":[],"buy_below":15.0,"vc":{"base":17.65,"base_src":"dcf","bear":11.45,"bull":26.76,"alt_median":22.92,"n_alt":2,"gap":-0.2297,"dispersion":0.2865,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":17.7245,"ev_ebitda":10.514,"pfcf":15.7535,"pb":2.1712,"roic":0.127,"gross_margin":0.3467,"fcf_margin":0.0625,"div_yield":0.0235}},"mc_quantiles":[7.31,10.07,11.45,12.43,13.35,14.23,15.11,15.72,16.38,17.08,17.86,18.6,19.34,20.11,21.17,21.92,23.48,24.92,26.76,29.83,37.4],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.43,"discount_rate":0.479,"terminal_growth":0.029,"exit_multiple":0.062},"ticker":"VVV","date":"2026-11-20"}